      "calculationScope": "EXACT_MANUAL_CALCULATION",
      "manualArithmetic": "Actual source SVG: triangle peak40N at0.10s and zero endpoints0/0.20s. Each half has impulse(1/2)(1/10)40=2N*s; total4N*s and average4/(1/5)=20N, below40N. Signed component areas give signed impulse. Sum two Newton equations: internal forces cancel, external impulse alone changes total momentum. Reviewer collision probe only: masses2,1kg and velocities+3,-1m/s give p=5kg*m/s, sticking vf=5/3m/s, Ki=19/2J,Kf=25/6J,loss16/3J. General sticking loss is half reduced mass times relative speed squared; elastic root is derived from momentum and kinetic energy equations. No decimal calculator work or student calibration claimed.",
      "manualFeasibility": "PASS_AI_EXACT",
      "physicalAssumptions": "Classical inertial frame and constant constituent masses. Vector impulse, average force and signed areas are componentwise; positive contact duration. Momentum conservation requires negligible external impulse for the chosen system/component. Internal action-reaction pairs belong to different bodies. Sticking shares one velocity; elastic collision preserves total kinetic energy; ordinary inelastic transfer may enter internal energy. No assumption that every collision conserves kinetic energy.",
      "pedagogicalReview": "Connects rapid variable force to impulse rather than substituting peak force for mean force. Actual triangular SVG makes4N*s and20N manually available. Introduces system selection, external impulse and componentwise conservation before collision equations. Requires signed velocities and distinguishes elastic energy conservation from sticking/internal conversion. No choice options or empirical student calibration.",
